endobj
574 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 366 0 R
/E (So how do we fix that? How can we take steps to remove stupidity on a personal level, and also from society as a whole? Well the first thing to do is resolve our ignorance about the danger of stupidity, which those of you who read the article this far have already done \(yeah, I am cool just like that\). The next thing we can do is to train ourselves to question, scrutinize and modify our beliefs on a regular basis. We can learn to accept constructive criticism of our values and beliefs from others as well, without feeling attacked or needing to defend ourselves. This is made easier by reminding ourselves that we are not defined by a set of strict beliefs, and criticism of those beliefs is not a criticism of our character or identity. We can take a step even further and choose to wilfully seek out those who will critique our beliefs and ideas and dispute our convictions. On an interpersonal level, we can be less accepting of stupidity and take steps to not only resolve our own stupidity and ignorance, but also contribute to resolving the stupidity of those around us. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
575 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 366 0 R
/E (Ultimately, overcoming stupidity isn't about being the smartest person in the room but rather about being aware of how little you know and spending a lifetime trying to resolve that. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
