/T (There is something almost perversely fascinating about Elijah Mikaelson because he is constructed around contradiction. He is one of the most cultured, articulate and self-controlled characters in The Vampire Diaries and The Originals, yet he is also capable of extraordinary violence; he speaks constantly about morality while repeatedly violating it; he presents himself as the guardian of his family while sometimes becoming its most dangerous weapon; and he spends centuries attempting to preserve the people he loves even when those people repeatedly make that love almost impossible. )
/E (There is something almost perversely fascinating about Elijah Mikaelson because he is constructed around contradiction. He is one of the most cultured, articulate and self-controlled characters in The Vampire Diaries and The Originals, yet he is also capable of extraordinary violence; he speaks constantly about morality while repeatedly violating it; he presents himself as the guardian of his family while sometimes becoming its most dangerous weapon; and he spends centuries attempting to preserve the people he loves even when those people repeatedly make that love almost impossible. )
/Pg 21 0 R
