/E (Elijah has spent centuries constructing himself into the man who can remain standing when everyone else falls apart. If Klaus \(his younger brother\) is the storm, Elijah becomes the person who walks into the storm carrying an umbrella, a first-aid kit, a legal document and somehow still manages to look devastatingly handsome \(whoops\). His refinement therefore functions partly as emotional regulation and partly as identity construction. He has decided who he must be and then he disciplines himself relentlessly into becoming that person. )
