/T (Parentification occurs when a child assumes responsibilities that developmentally belong to the adults around them, becoming a caretaker, mediator or stabilising figure within the family. Elijah repeatedly occupies precisely this role. He becomes one of the siblings who attempts to maintain order, particularly in relation to Klaus. Instead of simply being Klaus's brother, Elijah gradually becomes something closer to his protector, mediator, moral guide and emotional regulator. This is significant because the psychological relationship between the brothers is not simply one of affection. Elijah's identity becomes intertwined with Klaus's survival.)
