/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 370 0 R
/E (The problem with codependency is that love can gradually become indistinguishable from responsibility. Elijah repeatedly behaves as though Klaus's choices are somehow his burden to manage. If Klaus becomes violent, Elijah tries to intervene. If Klaus is threatened, Elijah protects him. If Klaus becomes emotionally isolated, Elijah tries to reconnect him with the family. If Klaus destroys something, Elijah frequently finds himself attempting to rebuild it. At some point, one desperately wants to tell this thousand-year-old vampire: sir, your brother is responsible for his own decisions.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
599 0 obj
