/E (Perhaps Elijah's greatest tragedy is that he spends so much of his life trying to become the person his family needs that he gradually loses sight of the person he himself might have wanted to be. He carries everyone else's fear so that they can remain fearless. He absorbs their chaos so that they can experience stability. He forgives because someone has to. He protects because someone has to. He stays because someone has to.)
/Pg 30 0 R
