/E (Perhaps the most important thing to understand about Elijah is that, for all his wisdom, restraint and centuries of experience, there was one promise from which he never learned to walk away: Always and Forever. It was not merely a childhood vow shared between siblings; it became the foundation of his identity, the psychological contract around which he built his entire existence. )
/Pg 30 0 R
