/E (Klaus once called Elijah a master of forgiveness. Perhaps he was. But Elijah's greatest gift was not forgiveness. It was devotion: the extraordinary, sometimes beautiful and sometimes deeply destructive ability to remain when everyone else had left. He spent his life believing that family was something you protected even when it hurt, that love was something you honoured even when it cost you and that the people you called your own should never have to face the darkness alone.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [5]
