713 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 382 0 R
/E (There is no single legal definition of a cult, but psychologists generally describe it as a group that exercises excessive control over its members through emotional, psychological or social manipulation. Healthy communities encourage questioning of their belief system, support personal interest or choices and exercise communication with our individuals. Cults often do the opposite. They discourage questions and impose their choices on you as if they were your own, they make following the leader more prevalent than our own wishes.  The danger is not unusual beliefs alone. Many harmless groups have uncommon beliefs. The real warning sign is when a group controls how people think, feel or make decisions. )
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [7]
>>
