/E (Psychologist Abraham Maslow's Hierarchy of Needs explains that humans naturally seek love, belonging, and purpose after their basic needs are met. During emotionally difficult periods, such as loneliness, grief, family conflict or uncertainty about the future, these needs become even stronger. Cults often appear during exactly these vulnerable moments.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
