/E (One of psychology's most famous experiments was conducted by Stanley Milgram. Participants believed they were giving painful electric shocks to another person because an authority instructed them to continue. Many obeyed even when they appeared deeply uncomfortable. The study suggested something unsettling: ordinary people often obey authority more than they expect. Inside cults, leaders become powerful authority figures. When obedience becomes connected with morality, followers may perform actions they would have rejected before joining. )
