/E (     While traditional learning often forces a step-by-step, inside-out approach to problem-solving, dyslexic cognition works from the outside in. It grasps complex, interconnected systems as a single, holistic ecosystem. In fields like architecture, industrial design, engineering and storytelling, this ability to zoom out and synthesize massive amounts of spatial information makes dyslexic thinkers remarkably inventive. They spot overarching narratives, structural flaws and big-picture possibilities long before linear analysis catches up.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [8]
>>
