908 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 402 0 R
/E (The butterflies therefore aren't a perfect message from the universe and they aren't proof that something is destined to happen. They mean something much simpler: your brain has decided that this moment matters \(traitor x3\). And maybe that's what makes butterflies so fascinating. A person who was once a complete stranger can slowly become someone your brain searches for in a crowded room, someone whose message can change your mood, someone whose presence makes your nervous system react before you've even had time to think. The same nervous system can make your stomach flutter before you confess your feelings, before you step onto a stage, before you open an important result, before you meet someone new or before you take a risk that matters to you. We call it falling in love, feeling nervous, being excited or simply having a gut feeling. Science calls it neural activity, hormones, reward, attachment, attention, arousal and emotion.)
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
