/E (The Real World is nothing like Barbieland. Barbie discovers what it means to be a woman in a world where women don't automatically hold positions of power. Ken, however, discovers patriarchy. He becomes fascinated by the idea that men can hold power just because they are men. When he returns to Barbieland, he transforms it into Kendom. The Barbies lose their independence and the Kens take control.)
