919 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 403 0 R
/E (When I first watched Barbie, I expected a fun, pink movie. And it was. The outfits, the music, the humour, Ryan Gosling's Ken. Everything was entertaining. But somewhere between the jokes and the ridiculously pink sets, I found myself thinking about things I hadn't expected to think. The thing that stayed with me wasn't the ending or even the plot. It was the idea that we spend so much of our lives trying to become the version of ourselves that everyone else expects us to be. Barbie is expected to be perfect. Ken is expected to be Barbie's boyfriend. Just like as students, we are expected to get excellent grades, maintain friendships, plan our futures and somehow remain completely unaffected by the stress of it all. So naturally, sometimes it feels like whatever we do, we are always failing one expectation while meeting another.)
/Pg 57 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
