934 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 406 0 R
/T (One of the stories that stayed with me was that of an elderly man who had begun to see himself as worthless. His feelings were deeply connected to his family and to the belief that he had failed to achieve anything meaningful in his life. He felt as though he had not accomplished enough and because of this, had gradually begun to see himself as a useless person. From the outside, such thoughts might seem irrational or even easy to dismiss. Someone might say that he had lived an entire life and that surely the experiences he had collected over all those years were achievements in themselves. But psychology reminds us that self-worth is not)
/E (One of the stories that stayed with me was that of an elderly man who had begun to see himself as worthless. His feelings were deeply connected to his family and to the belief that he had failed to achieve anything meaningful in his life. He felt as though he had not accomplished enough and because of this, had gradually begun to see himself as a useless person. From the outside, such thoughts might seem irrational or even easy to dismiss. Someone might say that he had lived an entire life and that surely the experiences he had collected over all those years were achievements in themselves. But psychology reminds us that self-worth is not)
/Pg 60 0 R
/K [2]
>>
