994 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 415 0 R
/E (The most vital aspect of a gratitude journal is to practice honesty with yourself. Try not to overinflate things because you might feel disappointed later on. It is always advisable to refrain from using the same sentence structure when writing every day. If you are always grateful for the family, for instance, try to find specific reasons for being grateful instead of using the same sentence. Avoid getting stuck writing a lot or too long sentences when making entries into your journal. A good entry can sometimes be made by writing three simple sentences. Finally, always try to put pen to paper or fingertips to the keyboard every day. If something happens and you do not make an entry, it should not stop you from continuing. )
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
