/E (   Early on he exhibited solitary behaviour, while he also had a great need to meet the Christian duties of charity. He idealized family life, but he failed to marry and to found a family himself despite having several, although problematic, love affairs. Living with family or artists was the only alternative, but in both respects he was no ideal partner. He showed self-neglect and self-destructive behaviour \(drinking too much alcohol combined with malnutrition\), self-mutilation \(the ear incident, possible self-poisoning and ultimately he committed a suicide attempt that resulted in his death\). )
/Pg 73 0 R
/K [4]
