/E (    No diagnosis can fully contain a life as complicated as his, nor can a medical label explain the strange beauty of The Starry Night, the tenderness of The Potato Eaters, or the quiet humanity scattered throughout his work. His suffering may have shaped the way he saw the world, but it was not the entirety of what he saw. There was also wonder, compassion, longing, hope and an almost desperate desire to find meaning in existence.)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [6]
