/E ( Most importantly, football offers multiple levels of identification simultaneously. A person can identify with a player, a club, a city, a country, a generation or even a particular style of play. Someone can admire Messi while supporting Real Madrid, love Ronaldo while supporting Argentina, follow a Premier League club while cheering for India in cricket and still somehow maintain the conviction that their sporting opinions are completely rational. Human identity is complicated enough to accommodate all of this. Football's greatest psychological advantage may therefore be combination. It is easy enough to understand that a child can follow it and complex enough that an expert can spend a lifetime analysing it. It is individual enough to create heroes and collective enough to create tribes. It is unpredictable enough to generate suspense but structured enough to produce meaningful narratives. It can be played almost anywhere, watched almost everywhere and discussed by almost everyone. Most importantly, football offers multiple levels of identification simultaneously. A person can identify with a player,)
