/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 436 0 R
/E (Nostalgia often becomes stronger during periods of transition. Graduating school. Moving cities. Losing a friendship. Starting college. Growing older. Leaving behind a familiar routine. When the present feels uncertain, the past can feel incredibly stable. You already know how that story ends. You know the people who were there. You know what those places looked like. You know who you were. The future, however, is full of unanswered questions. And the human brain doesn't always enjoy uncertainty. So sometimes, we look backwards because looking forwards feels frightening.)
/Pg 90 0 R
/K [1]
>>
