/Title (Suddenly, checking your phone isn't just checking your phone. Your brain is looking for the possibility of a reward, wondering whether that person's name might appear on the screen or whether the next interaction might bring another moment of excitement. This is also one reason unpredictable attention can sometimes feel particularly powerful. When someone is sometimes affectionate, sometimes distant and sometimes unexpectedly attentive, each positive interaction may feel more significant because it is less predictable \(keep them guessing\).)
